## Getting Started

```bash
npm install nodemailer   ← new dependency for email verification
npm run dev              # starts with nodemon on port 3000
```

Server runs at `http://localhost:3000`.

---

## API Endpoints

### Auth Routes — `/api/auth`

| Method | Endpoint | Auth Required | Role | Description |
|--------|----------|---------------|------|-------------|
| POST | `/api/auth/register` | No | — | Create account + send verification email |
| GET | `/api/auth/verify-email/:token` | No | — | Verify email via token link |
| POST | `/api/auth/login` | No | — | Login (verified users only) |
| GET | `/api/auth/get-me` | Yes | any | Get currently logged-in user info |
| POST | `/api/auth/refresh-token` | No (cookie) | — | Issue new access + refresh tokens |
| PATCH | `/api/auth/update-role` | Yes | admin | Change another user's role |

### Delete Routes — `/api/dele`

| Method | Endpoint | Auth Required | Role | Description |
|--------|----------|---------------|------|-------------|
| DELETE | `/api/dele/users/:id` | Yes | admin | Delete a user by MongoDB `_id` |

---

## How It Works

### Register
- Validated by `validateRegister` middleware
- Checks for duplicate email or username
- Hashes password with bcrypt (10 salt rounds)
- Creates user with `role: 'user'` and `isVerified: false` by default
- Generates a random verification token using `crypto`
- Sends verification email with a link to `/verify-email/:token`
- Returns success message — **no tokens issued at register**

### Verify Email
- User clicks link in email → `GET /api/auth/verify-email/:token`
- Finds user by verification token in DB
- Sets `isVerified: true` and clears `verificationToken`
- User can now login

### Login
- Validated by `validateLogin` middleware
- Looks up user by email
- **Blocks login if `isVerified: false`** — returns `401`
- Compares password against bcrypt hash
- Generates 15-minute access token and 7-day refresh token
- Saves refresh token to DB
- Sets refresh token in httpOnly cookie
- Returns access token and role in response body

### Get Me
- Protected by `authentication` middleware
- Returns `username`, `email`, and `role` from `req.user`

### Refresh Token
1. Reads refresh token from httpOnly cookie
2. Verifies token signature and expiry
3. Finds user in DB
4. Compares token against stored DB token — mismatch returns `401`
5. Generates new access + refresh tokens (rotation)
6. Saves new refresh token to DB, invalidating the old one
7. Sets new cookie and returns new access token

### Change Role (admin only)
- Protected by `authentication` + `adminOnly` middleware
- Validated by `validateChangeRole` middleware
- Accepts `userId` and `role` in request body
- Updates target user's role in DB

### Delete User (admin only)
- Protected by `authentication` + `adminOnly` middleware
- Deletes target user by `req.params.id`
- Prevents admin from deleting their own account

