## Testing with Postman

### Register
```
POST /api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "username": "john_doe",
    "email": "john@example.com",
    "password": "secure1"
}

→ 201: { "message": "User registered successfully. Please verify your email." }
→ 400: { "message": "Username must be between 3 and 20 characters" }
```

### Verify Email
```
GET /api/auth/verify-email/<token from email link>

→ 200: { "message": "Email verified successfully. You can now login." }
→ 400: { "message": "Invalid verification token" }
```

### Login
```
POST /api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "john@example.com",
    "password": "secure1"
}

→ 200: { "message": "Login successful", "token": "<accessToken>", "role": "user" }
→ 401: { "message": "Please verify your email before logging in" }
→ Cookie set: refreshToken (httpOnly)
```

### Get Me
```
GET /api/auth/get-me
Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>

→ 200: { "message": "User fetched successfully", "user": { "username": "...", "email": "...", "role": "..." } }
→ 401: { "message": "Token expired" }
```

### Refresh Token
```
POST /api/auth/refresh-token
(refreshToken cookie sent automatically)

→ 200: { "message": "Token refreshed successfully", "token": "<newAccessToken>" }
```

### Change Role (admin only)
```
PATCH /api/auth/update-role
Authorization: Bearer <adminAccessToken>
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "userId": "<target MongoDB _id>",
    "role": "manager"
}

→ 200: { "message": "Role updated successfully" }
→ 400: { "message": "Invalid user ID format" }
→ 403: { "message": "Forbidden" }
```

### Delete User (admin only)
```
DELETE /api/dele/users/<userId>
Authorization: Bearer <adminAccessToken>

→ 200: { "message": "User deleted successfully" }
→ 400: { "message": "You cannot delete yourself" }
→ 403: { "message": "Forbidden" }
```

---

## Full Auth Flow

```
POST /register
    ├── account created, role: 'user', isVerified: false
    └── verification email sent

GET /verify-email/:token
    └── isVerified: true

POST /login (unverified)
    └── 401 Please verify your email

POST /login (verified)
    ├── access token  → response body (15 mins)
    └── refresh token → httpOnly cookie (7 days)

GET /get-me
    └── Authorization: Bearer <accessToken> → returns user data

Access token expires
    └── POST /refresh-token
            ├── cookie verified against DB
            ├── new access + refresh tokens issued
            └── repeats every 15 mins

Refresh token expires (7 days)
    └── must POST /login again
```

---

## Security Summary

| Threat | Mitigation |
|--------|------------|
| XSS | Refresh token in httpOnly cookie — JS cannot read it |
| CSRF | `sameSite: strict` cookie flag |
| Token theft | Access token expires in 15 minutes |
| Stolen refresh token | Reuse detection — DB mismatch returns `401` |
| Brute force | bcrypt hashing slows password attacks |
| Privilege escalation | Role validated server-side on every admin action |
| Self-deletion | Admin cannot delete their own account |
| Invalid input | express-validator rejects malformed requests before controller |
| Fake accounts | Email verification required before login |